I've just uploaded gpm-0.9 to sunsite.unc.edu.

gpm is a "General Purpose Mouse" server and client library. It is meant
to run on the Linux console, but mouse-sensitive applications can
run under xterm without even recompiling.

The goal of the package is to ease the development of
curses application by providing an high level feel of mouse events.

CLIENTS
-------

The distribution embeds a sample client and an emacs package to use
the mouse under the text console. Dialog has been ported but the mods are
waiting to go in the mainstream release.

PORABILITY
----------

gpm-0.9 provides a sample portable client as well -- a C source with
an autoconf file and support sources to run under the Linux console or
under xterm without modification. It has been tested under SunOS, HP-UX,
Solaris, Ultrix and Linux (with and without libgpm, with and without X).

European Linuxers can download the package from iride.unipv.it:/pub/gpm
without waiting for the mirror sites.

Cheers,
