This is a reminder that comp.os.linux.announce is a moderated
newsgroup for Linux announcements only. I've been receiving a 
fair number of questions and other inappropriate submissions
for c.o.l.announce recently, and some readers may not be aware
that this newsgroup is moderated. Questions should be posted
to one of the other Linux newsgroups, such as comp.os.linux.help.

Please don't submit questions, requests for repostings, and 
so forth to c.o.l.announce. Rejecting these submissions wastes
my time. There are complete archives of c.o.l.announce available on 
sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/docs/linux-announce.archive. 

If you have problems submitting announcements to c.o.l.announce,
you can mail them directly to linux-announce@tc.cornell.edu. 
If your news software is correctly configured, posting announcements
using "Pnews" or a similar interface should mail the submission to
this address automatically. When in doubt, mail directly.

If you wish to get in touch with the moderators (myself and 
Lars Wirzenius) you can mail linux-announce-request@tc.cornell.edu.
This address is _not_ for mailing list or subscription requests.
If you wish to join the mailing list mirror of c.o.l.announce,
send mail to linux-activists-request@niksula.hut.fi with
the body
	X-Mn-Admin: join ANNOUNCE

Thanks much,
M. Welsh
Your friendly neighbourhood moderator 


