early comments and bugs in the distribution, I've made some updates.

First of all, if you've already downloaded the distribution and it
works (you've figured out the XCOMM -> # problem in XF86Config.eg)
there is no need to download it again. It's mainly a cleanup for
newer people to download.

CHANGES:
	Outlines changes made to the distribution.

INSTALL:
	Minor cosmetic changes made and an additional note made
	about fixing the wide-open toplevel directory permissions
	made by using the tar -p option.

SUMS:
FILES.gz:
	Updated with new values.

XF86-3.1-lib.tar.gz:
	I've fixed the XCOMM problem in XF86Config.eg.

XF86-3.1-bin.tar.gz:
	I've moved Xnest and Xvfb to the extra package. These are fun
	sample servers in X11R6 that most people don't care about.

XF86-3.1-extra.tar.gz:
	Contains the Xnest and Xvfb servers.

